description:
Edit repos/development-vessel/src/resolvers/docs-align-tick.ts to add one helper function. This is a single insertion; no existing line changes.

The exact line
function walkScripts(dir: string, cap: number): string[] {
occurs exactly once in this file. Insert the following complete function immediately BEFORE it, at top level with no indentation, and leave one blank line between the inserted function and walkScripts:

async function fetchAdvertisedShapes(): Promise<string[]> {
  const base = (process.env["DISCOVERY_ENDPOINT"] ?? "http://127.0.0.1:8100").replace(/\/+$/, "");
  try {
    const res = await fetch(`${base}/registry/shapes`, { signal: AbortSignal.timeout(10_000) });
    if (!res.ok) return [];
    const j = (await res.json()) as unknown;
    const arr = Array.isArray(j)
      ? j
      : Array.isArray((j as { shapes?: unknown })?.shapes)
        ? (j as { shapes: unknown[] }).shapes
        : [];
    return arr.filter((s): s is string => typeof s === "string");
  } catch {
    return [];
  }
}

No import statement is needed — process.env and fetch are globals, and the file already imports what it uses. Do not add or modify any import.

PURPOSE: this supplies the missing input for the accuracy invariant in docs-align-scan.ts. That branch is gated at docs-align-scan.ts line 236 on pointer.live_truth.advertised_shapes. docs-align-tick.ts line 184 currently builds live_truth as { existing_paths, unit_names } only, both from the local filesystem, exactly as its own comment at line 167 says: "Assemble live_truth from local filesystem only". Because the tick never queries the discovery registry, advertised_shapes is always undefined, so the accuracy check — the only invariant that compares a document against live truth — has never once executed. A separate later change will pass this into live_truth and add "accuracy" to the invariants array. Do NOT make that change now.

Every failure path returns an empty array on purpose, so if discovery is unreachable the accuracy branch stays exactly as inert as it is today instead of throwing. This mirrors an idiom the vessel already uses: orphaned-capability-scan.ts and residual-shape-discovery.ts both fetch discovery with the same `.replace(/\/+$/, "")` normalisation.

Do NOT modify walkScripts, walkMd, deriveNamingVocabulary, resolveDocsAlignTick, the live_truth object literal, or the invariants array.

